      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1745814312126,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Suppose character 'a' appears 5 times.\n5 / 2 = 2 \n2 * 2 = 4\n\nSo, we can use 4 'a's to form pairs (2 on left and 2 on right).\n1 'a' is left unpaired.\n\nc: 4/2 = 2 → 4 used\n\nit means c occures 4 times in string, from which we can form 2 pairs\nhence divide count/2 and then multiply by 2 to find how many pairs can\nbe formed.\n\nHence, To form a palindrome, we need pairs of characters —because one character must\ngo on the left side and the same character on the right side.\n\nIf any character appears an odd number of times,then we can use all of its even part\nfor pairs,and only one extra character can sit in the center.",
      "fontSize": 43,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Suppose character 'a' appears 5 times.\n5 / 2 = 2 \n2 * 2 = 4\n\nSo, we can use 4 'a's to form pairs (2 on left and 2 on right).\n1 'a' is left unpaired.\n\nc: 4/2 = 2 → 4 used\n\nit means c occures 4 times in string, from which we can form 2 pairs\nhence divide count/2 and then multiply by 2 to find how many pairs can\nbe formed.\n\nHence, To form a palindrome, we need pairs of characters —because one character must go on the left side and the same character on the right side.\n\nIf any character appears an odd number of times,then we can use all of its even part for pairs,and only one extra character can sit in the center.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "LJELXA9ZHRjQja-OffRbs",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -217.8286251520302,
      "y": 57815.683478884916,
      "width": 1485.5317742036113,
      "height": 2365,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
